note BYN1080: `find(xs, at: 3) is { } k` binds an optional with a pattern; the miss leaves, so a
`let` can bind it

  10 │     if (find(xs, at: 3) is { } k) {
     │        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ binds with a pattern
     │
  help: write `let k = find(xs, at: 3) ?? return 0`
     │ 10 │     let k = find(xs, at: 3) ?? return 0
     │    │     +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
     │ 11 │     let doubled = k * 2
     │    │ +++++++++++++++++++++++
     │ 12 │     return doubled
     │    │ ++++++++++++++++++

